## Verification layers

| Layer | Purpose | Canonical command | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|
| Fast feedback | Structural checks plus configured short commands | `./dev/check` | Terminal result and project output |
| Completion gate | One fixed Verification Run over required stages | `./dev/verify` | `.harness/runs/<run>-verify/manifest.json`, `gate.json`, `report.md`, check JSON, and available logs |
| Smoke or end-to-end | User-observable project behavior | `./dev/smoke` | Project-specific output under the same run when invoked by verify |

The completion gate executes security, document-catalog drift, documentation, plans/traceability, architecture, configured project verification, and optional smoke in a fixed order. `dev/harness.toml` is the project-owned source of configured commands.

## Check status and Gate

Checks record only:

- `pass`: the declared check completed successfully;
- `fail`: candidate behavior did not satisfy the check;
- `error`: configuration or infrastructure prevented reliable evidence;
- `skipped`: an optional check is correctly not configured; or
- `unknown`: evidence could not be determined and must not be treated as pass.

A required `fail` takes precedence over a required `error` or `unknown`. Missing configured tools and malformed configured smoke fail visibly. Artifacts are finalized as far as possible for success, candidate failure, and infrastructure error.

Gate classifies explicit local changed paths as `contained`, `wide`, `irreversible`, or `unknown` and returns `PASS`, `REVIEW`, `BLOCK`, or `INCONCLUSIVE`. Shadow mode may return zero for PASS/REVIEW while preserving the verdict; enforce mode returns zero only for PASS. BLOCK and INCONCLUSIVE are never overridden.

